    "content": "{\n  \"hypothesis\": \"Improve the performance of the OpenMP-based solution by optimizing the loop order and reducing the number of critical sections.\",\n  \"transformations\": [\"Optimize loop order\", \"Reduce critical sections\"],\n  \"sources_kept\": [],\n  \"files\": [\n    {\n      \"path\": \"src/solution.cpp\",\n      \"content\": \"/*\\n * Optimized solution with OpenMP directives\\n */\\n\\n#include <iostream>\\n#include <vector>\\n#include <cstdio>\\n#include <cassert>\\n#include <omp.h>\\n\\nint main() {\\n    int n, s;\\n    std::cin >> n >> s;\\n    std::vector<std::vector<int> > matrix(n, std::vector<int>(n));\\n    for(int i=0;i<n;i++)\\n        for(int j=0;j<n;j++) \\n            scanf(\\\"%d\\\", &(matrix[i][j]));\\n\\n    assert(s<n);\\n    assert(n<8000);\\n    assert(s>0);\\n    assert(n>0);\\n\\n    int sum = 0, mxSum = 0;\\n    #pragma omp parallel for reduction(max:mxSum)\\n    for(int i=0;i<s;i++) {\\n        for(int j=0;j<s;j++) {\\n            sum += matrix[i][j];\\n        }\\n        #pragma omp critical\\n        mxSum = std::max(mxSum,sum);\\n    }\\n\\n    printf(\\\"%d\\n\\\",mxSum);\\n}\\n\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"notes\": \"The solution now uses a single critical section to update mxSum, which reduces the overhead of critical sections.\",\n  \"research\": {\n    \"queries\": [\n      \"OpenMP loop order optimization\",\n      \"Reducing critical sections in OpenMP\"\n    ],\n    \"urls\": [\n      \"https://www.openmp.org/specs/latest/html/omp_3_1.html#sect_3_1_2\",\n      \"https://www.openmp.org/specs/latest/html/omp_3_1.html#sect_3_1_3\"\n    ]\n  }\n}"
